Z||000014||Alex4mula||09-19-2001||11:47 AM||||I'll be there too. My 1st! I'll arrive Dalton GA on Friday night. I'll drive from there to Cherokee area very early Saturday morning to arrive at 8:00AM. Anyone driving from that area? <P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Ronnie||09-19-2001||08:40 PM||||Hey Alex, why are you going to Dalton, seems a bit out of the way , unless of course it's family or something.||||reg||6
Z||000016||Wolfhound||09-20-2001||07:01 AM||||Here is a bit of new info I recieved this morning from David Hunter.<P><BR>Coy,<P>Sorry it took me so long to get back to you. I've been living at the office<BR>and only get to go home to sleep. Our internet connection was down today, to<BR>protect us from the virus that's going around. Here's the information you<BR>asked for...<P>We'll be starting the Run at 8:00 (eastern time) on Saturday morning. We'll<BR>be leaving from the parking lot next to the Cherokee Inn. The run takes<BR>about 4 hours of driving, not including the photo stops and breaks to<BR>stretch legs. It's about 140 miles if I remember right.<P>Having a CB radio helps keep in touch with the other drivers. We use channel<BR>12 mostly, Channel 14 if if the hills give off too much static. After we get<BR>back from the run, We'll have lunch at the Ponderosa and then give away door<BR>prizes back at the Cherokee Inn. The rest of the day we'll break up and hang<BR>out at the casinos or the hotels and talk or gamble. Ed Parks is there and<BR>he's always good for a Fiero conversation!<P>Sunday we'll head for Deal's Gap. We'll leave from the same parking lot at<BR>9:00. We'll start on the NC side. After that most of us will probably head<BR>home. Some may go to the Biltmore house or explore the rest of the Smokies<BR>or go back to the casinos.<P>I hope you'll be able to come up for the Run. We have a great group of folks<BR>that come and  we have a lot of fun.<P>David Hunter<BR>Alabama Fieros<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Alex4mula||09-20-2001||08:29 AM||||Ronnie;<BR>Yes. My wife relatives are in Dalton. She will stay there (pregnancy & curves don't mix) and I'll drive to Cherokee Saturday morning.<P>David provided me the route we will take. Here it is in case you arrive late and need to find the group:<P>..." The directions will be pretty simple. <BR>We’ll leave from the parking lot at the strip mall by the Cherokee Inn at 8:00. There is a Chevron gas station there with a Hardee’s attached to it. And a Best Western across the street. There is one main road going into the Cherokee reservation. The Cherokee Inn is a block or two down that road on the right. Very easy to find. Even I could find it without even looking for it.<BR>From Cherokee, we’ll get on the Blue Ridge Parkway (BRP), going North or East. Since the BRP ends in Cherokee, this is only one way to go! We’ll be on the BRP from mile marker 470 to about mile marker 410. The midway point is going to be the Pisgah Inn. There will be a few stops along the way to stretch our legs and take pictures. I haven’t really picked those for sure yet, but they are visible from the road. It will be hard to miss 30 or so Fieros.<BR>At the Pisgah Inn, We’ll backtrack a few miles and turn left towards 276. Then take a right to get onto North 276. After 12-19 miles, there will be a stoplight. There, take a left onto 215 South. Follow that very fun road until you get back onto the BRP. Take a right onto the BRP and that will guide us back into Cherokee. We’ll backtrack a pretty good distance on the BRP. I’m sure if you pass us going the opposite way, you hear lots of horn honking and see huge smiles and gets lots of people waving. <BR>It’s more fun and scenic than I’ve described.<BR>We’ll be on CB channel 12 or maybe 14. You’ll be able to hear us and find out where we are if you’re close. <BR>I hope this gives you enough to go on and you get this in time."...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Formula88||09-20-2001||12:09 PM||||Man, I want to GOOOO!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I gotta work this weekend.  Oh well, probably best since I need new rear tires.  Don't want to be pushing my baby through Deals Gap with bald rear tires.  <P>Oh, but I'm so gonna be there next year!  I should have the suspension fully redone by then and hopefully my 17" rims!  Oh, yeah!||||reg||9
Z||000019||Wolfhound||09-20-2001||12:58 PM||||I'm really looking forward to this! The recent events have left me confused,with so many mixed emotions.<BR> <BR>A part of me says "Stay Home"with friends and family as we await the next shoe to fall.<P>Another says if we change our direction and objectives they have won.<BR> <BR>I also need to see this massive and beautiful place that is so filled with life and so washed in time to get my perspective back.<P> Maybe it will help me sort things out.<BR>Peace!<BR>Coy<BR>||||reg||1
